Standards-Version: 4.5.1
# No npm here: it ships with nodejs, and Debian's npm package conflicts with it.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               nodejs (>= 22.13)
Homepage: https://github.com/wirenboard/wb-nodejs-service-template

Package: wb-nodejs-service-template
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         nodejs (>= 22.13)
Recommends: mosquitto
Description: Network traffic of the controller as a device
 Publishes a virtual device with the receive rate of a network interface, the
 peak rate since the last reset, the uptime of the service itself and a button
 that resets the peak, so the traffic of the controller is visible in the web
 interface and usable in rules.
 .
 Dependencies are vendored at build time, so the controller needs no network
 and no compilation.
 .
 The package doubles as the template a Node.js service of ours is started from.
